  "fact_or_context_to_reference": "Unique quotient and remainder, parity classes, even/odd decomposition, and congruence as divisibility of a difference; addition respects congruence for every positive modulus. Division gives periodic listings and repeated listings, while parity separates tagged lists and gives alternating-sign integer codes. Include the modulo-three pattern in the size-comparison example. Positive-integer divisibility is an order, its proper divisors have smaller natural value, and finite covers give divisor comparisons. Both natural-number parity classes are infinite and complementary; an odd square is odd, supporting the least-denominator irrationality argument. Residue classes modulo four are infinite and give the four independent Boolean cells; alternating even and odd indices split an infinite enumeration. Parity of points and finite cardinalities gives colouring examples, and both parity classes are unbounded."
